From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:04:51 -0500
Subject: feat: a Space with nothing awake shows its own page; a download's
 start is plain to see (S-396, S-400)

A Space with no row awake (tabs R66; GitHub issue 72): a sleep that left no
row of the active Space awake opened a New Tab there, and every sleep of the
last pin added a row. The window now shows the Space with no page: a
stand-in tab, which the sidebar does not list (SpaceModel::HidesTab) and no
verb takes, on chrome://stedding-space. The page is one centred column on
the Space's colour: "Nothing open in <Space>", the command bar's key, a tip
at a time with a drawing the page makes, and one line at the foot that
Stedding is free, open source and has no ads, with "support it" to GitHub
Sponsors, opened only on a click. It is faint until the pointer is over it,
follows the Space's name and colour, and fetches nothing. Another row shown
closes it; an address typed while it shows makes it an ordinary row. The
session and the closed-tab list keep none (ShouldTrackURLForRestore), and
the address field shows no address. A window without Spaces keeps the New
Tab.

The download's start (sidebar-panels Pn18): Chromium flew a 26 DIP icon to
the toolbar's downloads button, which the sidebar keeps hidden. In a window
with the sidebar, a 48 DIP chip now flies from the page's middle to the
sidebar's downloads button in 800 ms, shrinking and fading as it lands, and
the button rings once. With motion off only the ring shows, held still.
Windows without the sidebar's button keep Chromium's animation.

Why: the owner, 2026-11-02: a Space with nothing awake should show the
Space, not a new tab, as version A of the rendered mockups; and the
download's animation was too small to notice. Chosen by the maintainers on
2026-11-04: the tips are drawn rather than screenshots, and the chip.
Removable when: never as a feature.
